            <ArticleTitle>Chiari type I malformations in young adults: implications for the college health practitioner.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>757-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/07448481.2011.570400</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors describe 2 cases of Chiari type I malformation (CM-I) in students presenting to a college health center within a 6-month period. A review of CM-I, including epidemiology, typical presentation, evaluation, and management, is followed by a discussion of the clinical and functional implications of the disorder in an emerging adult population.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
